{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:13:00", "text": "That sounds like a solid fix, George. Thanks for taking care of this so quickly!", "utterranceID": "20261217-5-276aa"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-5-276aa"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:14:00", "text": "No problem, @eid_35e32fec. Let me know if you need any more details or if there's anything else I can help with.", "utterranceID": "20261217-6-4bf32"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-6-4bf32"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T12:59:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Memory Leak in Parameter Storage' has been resolved. 🎉", "utterranceID": "20261226-0-994f5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-0-994f5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:03:00", "text": "The issue was due to improper memory management in the parameter storage module, which caused a gradual memory leak. This led to the optimization engine losing track of parameter updates over time.", "utterranceID": "20261226-1-6545e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-1-6545e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:07:00", "text": "I've submitted a fix that ensures proper deallocation of memory after each parameter update cycle. This prevents memory exhaustion and maintains the integrity of parameter history. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/48", "utterranceID": "20261226-2-5e8ee"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-2-5e8ee"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:11:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_6a0f49ba! Thanks for addressing this so quickly. I'll review the PR shortly.", "utterranceID": "20261226-3-08037"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-3-08037"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:13:00", "text": "Thanks, Ian! Let me know if you have any questions or need further clarification on the changes.", "utterranceID": "20261226-4-37962"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-4-37962"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:16:00", "text": "Will do, George. This fix should help improve the stability of our optimization engine significantly.", "utterranceID": "20261226-5-69625"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-5-69625"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:21:00", "text": "Absolutely, Ian. Looking forward to seeing the improvements in our next round of tests.", "utterranceID": "20261226-6-1c133"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-6-1c133"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2027-01-24T01:40:00", "text": "Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with AutoTuneForce that need our attention. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20270123-0-c7d2b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270123-0-c7d2b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2027-01-24T01:41:00", "text": "First up, we have a 'Cache Invalidation Bug Causes Stale Data Usage'. The caching mechanism in the Data Ingestion API isn't invalidating outdated data properly. This is causing slower model adaptation and outdated predictions for CUST-0093. @eid_6a0f49ba, this one's for you. Can you take a look? 🙏", "utterranceID": "20270123-1-cbf06"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270123-1-cbf06"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2027-01-24T01:42:00", "text": "Got it! I'll dive into the caching mechanism and see what's causing the stale data issue. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍", "utterranceID": "20270123-2-6d572"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270123-2-6d572"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2027-01-24T01:44:00", "text": "Great, thanks! Next, we have a 'Data Parsing Error Leads to Incomplete Data Ingestion'. The Data Ingestion API is having trouble parsing certain data formats, leading to incomplete data for model optimization. This is affecting CUST-0065. @eid_04a698e5, can you handle this one? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20270123-3-5c113"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270123-3-5c113"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_04a698e5", "timestamp": "2027-01-24T01:48:00", "text": "Sure thing! I'll check the parsing logic and ensure we're handling all data formats correctly. Let's get this sorted for CUST-0065. 💪", "utterranceID": "20270123-4-259a7"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270123-4-259a7"}

