{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2542cff3", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T06:54:00", "text": "The CORS errors are occurring because the external applications trying to access our APIs are not on the list of authorized domains. This is a security measure to prevent unauthorized access.", "utterranceID": "20260916-2-0da6d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260916-2-0da6d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_14a5889d", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T06:58:00", "text": "@David Taylor Thanks for the update. So, it's not a bug but rather a security feature?", "utterranceID": "20260916-3-8419d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260916-3-8419d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch-force-504165"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2542cff3", "timestamp": "2026-09-16T07:00:00", "text": "Exactly, Charlie. It's a common misunderstanding. The CORS policy is intentionally restrictive to ensure that only pre-approved domains can access our APIs.", "utterranceID": "20260916-4-bd283"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260916-4-bd283"}
