{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T21:14:00", "text": "Hi team, I hope you're all doing well! 😊 I wanted to kick off a discussion about our proposed PR to optimize the GraphQL API. I've found some interesting open-source projects that have implemented similar performance enhancements. Let's dive in and see what we can learn! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261106-0-6eae0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261106-0-6eae0"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T21:18:00", "text": "First up, we have a PR from Apache Kafka titled 'Optimize Consumer Group Coordination'. This PR focuses on reducing latency and improving the efficiency of consumer group coordination. You can check it out here: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/4948. What do you think, @eid_8cbee5b3?", "utterranceID": "20261106-1-8986e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261106-1-8986e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8cbee5b3", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T21:22:00", "text": "Thanks, Emma! This Kafka PR is quite relevant. The way they handle consumer group coordination could give us insights into managing our data retrieval processes more efficiently. It might be worth exploring how they reduce latency. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261106-2-5960f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261106-2-5960f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_01e37306", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T21:24:00", "text": "Agreed, Fiona T. The focus on latency reduction is something we should definitely consider. It aligns well with our goal to improve load times for the GraphQL API. Maybe we can adapt some of their strategies. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20261106-3-2acec"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261106-3-2acec"}

{"title": "Implement Secure Handshake Protocol for Initial Connections", "summary": "This PR introduces a secure handshake protocol for establishing initial connections between clients and servers, ensuring the authenticity and integrity of the communication setup.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/CollaborateForce/pull/38", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "38", "state": "open", "user": {"login": "eid_7dfbbca2"}, "created_at": "2026-10-30T13:10:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_a88ee967"}, "comment": "The implementation aligns perfectly with TLS 1.3 standards. Great job!", "submitted_at": "2026-10-30T18:38:00"}, {"state": "COMMENTED", "user": {"login": "eid_abbf3651"}, "comment": "The initial connection tests are solid, maintaining authenticity and integrity. Well done!", "submitted_at": "2026-10-30T18:42:00"}, {"state": "COMMENTED", "user": {"login": "eid_4988ee2a"}, "comment": "Performance tests show acceptable latency, and the documentation is clear. Security benefits are well outlined. Nice work!", "submitted_at": "2026-10-30T18:47:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_CollaborateForce_pull_38"}
{"title": "Develop API Client Libraries for Popular Languages", "summary": "Create client libraries for popular programming languages to facilitate easy integration of CollaborateForce API into third-party applications.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/CollaborateForce/pull/39", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "39", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_76d9cb07"}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:58:00", "reviews": [{"state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "user": {"login": "eid_a1fab288"}, "comment": "The Python and JavaScript libraries look great with intuitive interfaces and clear documentation. However, the Java library needs additional usage examples in the documentation.", "submitted_at": "2026-11-01T06:33:00"}, {"state": "PENDING", "user": {"login": "eid_4d18a84c"}, "comment": "The libraries are well-documented, but the JavaScript library requires more comprehensive performance tests, including stress testing results to ensure it handles high loads effectively.", "submitted_at": "2026-11-01T06:40:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_CollaborateForce_pull_39"}
{"title": "Revert PR# 36: GraphQL Integration", "summary": "This revert is necessary due to a change in product direction. The focus has shifted towards enhancing our REST API, and the GraphQL integration no longer aligns with our current goals. Reverting this PR will help us maintain alignment with our updated product strategy.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/CollaborateForce/pull/40", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "40", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_724e1180"}, "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:58:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_8cbee5b3"}, "comment": "LGTM", "submitted_at": "2026-11-03T21:21:00"}, {"state": "PENDING", "user": {"login": "eid_86f94a48"}, "comment": "LGTM", "submitted_at": "2026-11-03T21:26:00"}, {"state": "PENDING", "user": {"login": "eid_446bc3ee"}, "comment": "Approved", "submitted_at": "2026-11-03T21:27:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_CollaborateForce_pull_40"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86f94a48", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:06:00", "text": "Great points, @eid_01e37306 and Julia! Next, let's look at Hasura. They've implemented a GraphQL engine to handle real-time data queries and mutations. Here's their PR: https://github.com/hasura/graphql-engine/pull/4883. What do you think? 🤓", "utterranceID": "20260726-4-10243"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-4-10243"}
