{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df5d4b7", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:28:00", "text": "First up, we have Apache Kafka's feature: Draft API Endpoints for Topic Message Retrieval. They designed endpoints to retrieve messages from Kafka topics for downstream processing. You can check it out here: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/2125. What do you think, @eid_443fee06?", "utterranceID": "20260626-1-f8730"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-1-f8730"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_443fee06", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:30:00", "text": "Thanks, Bob! Kafka's approach seems robust, especially for high-throughput environments. Their focus on downstream processing aligns well with our sentiment analysis goals. We might want to consider their scalability strategies. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260626-2-5f487"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-2-5f487"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_31cb6db5", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:31:00", "text": "Agreed, David. Kafka's design could offer us some insights into handling large volumes efficiently. But we should also think about how our use case might differ, especially since we're dealing with Slack messages.", "utterranceID": "20260626-3-4fedf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-3-4fedf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df5d4b7", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:33:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's look at RabbitMQ's feature: Queue Message Retrieval API. They introduced endpoints to fetch messages from RabbitMQ queues for integration with analytics tools. Here's the link: https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/pull/2126. Thoughts, Ian?", "utterranceID": "20260626-4-23c0b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-4-23c0b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_31cb6db5", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:38:00", "text": "RabbitMQ's focus on analytics integration is interesting. It might be useful for us to consider how they handle message acknowledgment and retries. This could be crucial for ensuring we don't miss any Slack messages during processing. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260626-5-a7ce4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-5-a7ce4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_443fee06", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:39:00", "text": "Yeah, Ian, that's a good point. Their approach to message acknowledgment could help us maintain data integrity. We should definitely dive deeper into their implementation.", "utterranceID": "20260626-6-2eade"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-6-2eade"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df5d4b7", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:41:00", "text": "Finally, let's discuss Redis's feature: Stream Message Fetch API. They implemented endpoints to retrieve messages from Redis streams for real-time data processing. Check it out here: https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/2127. Any thoughts, team?", "utterranceID": "20260626-7-64d11"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-7-64d11"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_443fee06", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:42:00", "text": "Redis's real-time processing capabilities are impressive. This could be beneficial for our sentiment analysis, especially if we want to provide near-instant feedback. We should consider how they manage stream offsets and consumer groups.", "utterranceID": "20260626-8-b06de"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-8-b06de"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_31cb6db5", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:47:00", "text": "Absolutely, David. Redis's approach to real-time data could really enhance our feature. We might want to explore how they handle scaling with multiple consumers.", "utterranceID": "20260626-9-b0de2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-9-b0de2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-charliegarcia-SentimentForce", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-d38149"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4df5d4b7", "timestamp": "2026-06-26T15:52:00", "text": "Awesome insights, everyone! I'll take a closer look at these features and see how we can adapt some of their strategies for our implementation. Let's aim to incorporate the best practices from these projects. Thanks for the input! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260626-10-a591d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260626-10-a591d"}

{"Channel": {"name": "planning-imentAIX", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-141b6b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d96fb219", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T02:59:00", "text": "Hey George, for the sentiment analysis misinterpretation, I think we should expand the NLP Engine section to include a focus on sarcasm and humor detection. We might need to incorporate additional datasets that include these elements. Thoughts, @eid_5890ce38?", "utterranceID": "20260422-1-808a1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260422-1-808a1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-imentAIX", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-141b6b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_2470307f", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T03:01:00", "text": "Agreed, Emma. We should also mention the need for contextual analysis in the NLP Engine section. This could help differentiate between literal and sarcastic statements. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260422-2-f08a1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260422-2-f08a1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-imentAIX", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-141b6b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_5890ce38", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T03:03:00", "text": "Great points, @eid_d96fb219 and @eid_2470307f. Let's add a subsection under NLP Engine for sarcasm and humor detection, and emphasize the need for contextual analysis. Next, about the Slack integration issues?", "utterranceID": "20260422-3-7bd7a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260422-3-7bd7a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-imentAIX", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-141b6b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_802e8eff", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T03:04:00", "text": "For Slack integration, we should update the Slack Integration section to include strategies for handling API rate limits and connectivity issues. Perhaps we can suggest implementing a retry mechanism and better error monitoring. @eid_5890ce38, does that sound good?", "utterranceID": "20260422-4-9c350"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260422-4-9c350"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-imentAIX", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-141b6b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_5346d7a5", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T03:09:00", "text": "Yes, and maybe we should also consider optimizing the third-party libraries we use for real-time data processing. This could be added to the Technical section. 🔧", "utterranceID": "20260422-5-139ea"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260422-5-139ea"}
{"Channel": {"name": "planning-imentAIX", "channelID": "ch-ntaix-141b6b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_5890ce38", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T03:11:00", "text": "Perfect, @eid_802e8eff and @eid_5346d7a5. Let's make those updates. Now, regarding the UI, any suggestions?", "utterranceID": "20260422-6-4d67c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260422-6-4d67c"}
