{"title": "Add Support for New Sensor Protocols", "summary": "Implement support for additional sensor protocols to enhance device compatibility. This PR focuses on updating the device layer to recognize and process data from newly identified sensor types.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/1", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "1", "state": "open", "user": {"login": "eid_2347b567"}, "created_at": "2026-09-26T08:53:00", "reviews": [{"state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "user": {"login": "eid_4df3bcc2"}, "comment": "The device layer updates look solid and recognize the new protocols well. However, the unit tests don't cover all the new sensor protocols. Please add those tests.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-26T16:15:00"}, {"state": "PENDING", "user": {"login": "eid_4b38019b"}, "comment": "Great work on the implementation! The documentation needs more detail on the new protocols supported. Please expand on that section.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-26T16:21:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_1"}
{"title": "Initialize RESTful API Framework", "summary": "Set up the foundational structure for the RESTful API framework, including necessary libraries and configurations to support API development.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/2", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "2", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_54905dcb"}, "created_at": "2026-09-29T03:54:00", "reviews": [{"state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "user": {"login": "eid_edf6a3fc"}, "comment": "The project structure looks solid and the libraries are well-chosen and configured. Nice work on that front! Once you add the basic GET endpoint, it should meet all the acceptance criteria.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-29T08:33:00"}, {"state": "COMMENTED", "user": {"login": "eid_4df3bcc2"}, "comment": "The setup is clean and organized. However, the server setup doesn't handle HTTP requests yet. Please include a basic endpoint for testing.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-29T08:30:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_2"}
{"title": "Implement JWT Token Generation and Validation", "summary": "This PR introduces the functionality to generate and validate JWT tokens for user authentication. It includes the creation of a utility module for handling JWT operations such as token creation, signing, and verification.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/3", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "3", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_3e076e53"}, "created_at": "2026-10-01T05:04:00", "reviews": [{"state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "user": {"login": "eid_bac7c6c4"}, "comment": "The JWT token generation and validation look solid. However, please update the documentation with usage instructions for the JWT utility.", "submitted_at": "2026-10-01T11:59:00"}, {"state": "COMMENTED", "user": {"login": "eid_4b38019b"}, "comment": "The core functionality is in place, but please add unit tests for edge cases like token expiration and invalid signatures to ensure robustness.", "submitted_at": "2026-10-01T11:58:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_3"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3e076e53", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T19:51:00", "text": "Great points! I'll dive deeper into their implementation and see what we can learn. Next, let's look at Apache Kafka's feature: 'JWT Authentication for Kafka Brokers'. This PR introduces JWT authentication to secure communication between Kafka brokers and clients. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/3179", "utterranceID": "20261114-4-4fd8a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261114-4-4fd8a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_edf6a3fc", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T19:53:00", "text": "Kafka's focus on securing broker-client communication is interesting. While our use case is a bit different, their approach to token validation and security might offer some valuable insights. 🔒", "utterranceID": "20261114-5-00782"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261114-5-00782"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bac7c6c4", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T19:54:00", "text": "True, Fiona. Even though our architecture differs, understanding their security measures could help us enhance our own JWT handling. Let's keep this in mind as we move forward.", "utterranceID": "20261114-6-1d746"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261114-6-1d746"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3e076e53", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T19:57:00", "text": "Absolutely! I'll make a note to explore their security protocols further. Lastly, we have Kubernetes' feature: 'JWT Token Authentication for API Server'. This PR updates the Kubernetes API server to authenticate requests using JWT tokens. Check it out here: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/3180", "utterranceID": "20261114-7-aaeb8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261114-7-aaeb8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce", "channelID": "ch-f_aix-a13a7a"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bac7c6c4", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T20:02:00", "text": "Kubernetes' implementation is quite relevant to us since we're also dealing with API authentication. Their method of integrating JWT into the API server could provide a solid reference for our own integration. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261114-8-eddd7"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261114-8-eddd7"}
